course: dictionary
lesson: 14653
title: Predation: the hunter and the hunted
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Predation is when one animal, the predator, hunts, kills and eats another animal, which is its prey. «The owl practises predation at night, hunting mice in the field.» The owl is the predator, and the mice are its prey.
explain: Predation is a noun that does not change into a plural, so we say predation, not predations. Look for the clues in the sentence: hunting and eating tell you what predation means, even if you have never met the word before.
explain: Predation keeps animal numbers balanced. «If the foxes disappear, the rabbits may grow far too many.» Without predators, prey animals can multiply until there is not enough food for all of them.
fact: Predation means one animal hunts, kills and eats another animal.
fact: The animal doing the hunting is the predator, and the animal being hunted is the prey.
fact: Prey animals avoid predation with camouflage, speed, shells, warning colours and living in groups.
fact: «Predation» keeps the numbers of prey animals in balance in a food chain.
fact: Conservation groups protect nests from predation by foxes and rats, so more chicks survive.
exercise: «The owl practises predation at night.» What is predation? | An animal changes colour to match its surroundings | *One animal hunts, kills and eats another animal | An animal sleeps all winter | Two animals share a home and food
exercise: «Zebras stay in large herds to avoid predation.» What does avoid predation mean? | Make a loud noise to scare the birds | Move to a new land | Find more food to eat | *Stay safe from being hunted and eaten
exercise: In a pond, a heron catches and eats a small frog. Which animal is the prey? | The heron | The pond | The sun | *The frog
test: Which word means one animal hunting and eating another? | Camouflage | Migration | Shelter | *Predation
test: In predation, what is the prey? | The animal that does the hunting | The place where animals sleep | The plants that grow in the ground | *The animal that gets hunted and eaten
exam: «Conservation groups protect nests from predation by foxes and rats.» Why do they do this? | *To keep the eggs and chicks safe from being eaten | To move the birds to a new country | To make the nests bigger | To give the foxes and rats more food
